e frequent exacerbations despite high-dose glucocorticoid therapy. Mepolizumab has shown promise in reducing exacerbation rates and improving lung function and quality of life in this population. However, if a Type 1 error were to occur, it would imply that the observed benefits of mepolizumab might be due to random chance rather than a true pharmacological effect. This could mislead clinicians into adopting a treatment that does not provide real benefits, potentially exposing patients to unnecessary risks without therapeutic gain. The importance of accurate statistical interpretation in clinical research is underscored, as it directly impacts treatment decisions and patient outcomes. \n"], "raw_output": "'''Option: B'''"}
